## Part 2: Data Sources — What, Why, and Where From

### At a Glance

| # | Data Source | What It Gives Us | How We Get It | Role |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **User's Survey Data** (magnetics) | Magnetic field measurements from the ground | 📁 **File upload** (XYZ/CSV/GRD/DAT/TIF, drag-and-drop) | Primary anomaly evidence — feeds the "magnetics" and "structure" scoring clues |
| 2 | **User's Geochemistry Data** | Soil sample lab results (gold, arsenic, etc.) | 📁 **File upload** (CSV) | Feeds the "geochemistry" scoring clue (the most heavily weighted) |
| 3 | **User's Assay Certificates** | Lab certificates confirming mineral grades | 📁 **File upload** (PDF) | Linked to spatial sample points — supports geochemistry |
| 4 | **Sentinel-2** (ESA satellite imagery) | Iron oxide, clay/hydroxyl, and vegetation indices | 🌐 **API** — Microsoft Planetary Computer STAC API | Alteration signature — feeds the lithology/alteration scoring |
| 5 | **Copernicus DEM GLO-30** (Digital Elevation Model) | Slope, hillshade, terrain | 🌐 **API** — Microsoft Planetary Computer STAC API | Terrain context and access (display layer, not scored) |
| 6 | **NOAA EMAG2v3** (Earth Magnetic Anomaly Grid) | Regional magnetic anomaly | 🌐 **API** — Remote COG (Cloud-Optimised GeoTIFF) file read via GDAL | Regional structural context (display layer, not primary scoring evidence — too coarse at ~2 arc-minute resolution) |
| 7 | **Macrostrat** | Rock types (lithology), geological age, structural units | 🌐 **API** — Macrostrat REST API (`macrostrat.org/api/v2/geologic_units/map`) | Feeds the "rock type" scoring clue — classifies rocks by gold-hosting favourability |
| 8 | **OneGeology / BRGM** (Bureau de Recherches Géologiques et Minières) | Geological map images | 🌐 **API** — WMS (Web Map Service) proxy to OneGeology/BRGM servers | Visual interpretation backdrop on the map (not scored) |
| 9 | **USGS MRDS** (United States Geological Survey — Mineral Resources Data System) | Known mineral deposits and occurrences | 📁 **Seeded file** — A curated seed of 14 real West African gold deposits is hardcoded in the codebase. Full MRDS load is planned. | Feeds the "nearby known deposits" scoring clue + verifies deposit names in generated reports |
| 10 | **WDPA** (World Database on Protected Areas) / Ghana Protected Areas | National parks, reserves, conservation boundaries | 📁 **Bundled GeoJSON file** — OSM-derived (OpenStreetMap), Ghana-clipped, shipped with the source code | Hard exclusion — cells inside protected areas are zeroed (not scored, vetoed) |
| 11 | **OpenStreetMap (OSM)** — Roads | Road network, highway classifications | 📁 **Bundled GeoJSON file** — OSM-derived Ghana road network, shipped with the source code | Access and logistics context (display layer) |

---

### Detailed Breakdown by Delivery Method

#### 📁 File Upload (User provides)

| Source | File Format | What Happens After Upload |
|---|---|---|
| Magnetics survey | XYZ, CSV, GRD, DAT, TIF (up to 500 MB) | Validated, checksummed, parsed, reprojected, kriged to a regular 50m grid, reduced to pole, depth estimated, written as a COG (Cloud-Optimised GeoTIFF) |
| Geochemistry | CSV | Column auto-detection, unit handling, deduplication, percentile thresholds (85th/95th/99th) computed per element from the project's own sample population |
| Assay certificates | PDF | Sample IDs and assay tables extracted, linked to spatial sample points by ID match |

#### 🌐 API (Platform fetches automatically to the licence boundary)

| Source | API / Protocol | Endpoint |
|---|---|---|
| Sentinel-2 L2A | STAC API (SpatioTemporal Asset Catalog) | `https://planetarycomputer.microsoft.com/api/stac/v1` — collection `sentinel-2-l2a` |
| Copernicus DEM GLO-30 | STAC API | `https://planetarycomputer.microsoft.com/api/stac/v1` — collection `cop-dem-glo-30` |
| NOAA EMAG2v3 | COG remote read via GDAL/rasterio | Configured URL in settings (`emag2_cog_url`) |
| Macrostrat geology | REST API (HTTP GET, JSON response) | `https://macrostrat.org/api/v2/geologic_units/map?lat=...&lng=...` |
| OneGeology / BRGM geology maps | WMS (Web Map Service) 1.1.1 `GetMap` | Configured URL in settings (`geology_wms_url`), proxied through our backend to fix CORS |

#### 📁 Bundled Files (Shipped with the application)

| Source | File | Location in Codebase |
|---|---|---|
| Ghana Protected Areas | `ghana_protected_areas.geojson` (OSM-derived, real boundaries) | `backend/app/data/ghana_protected_areas.geojson` |
| Ghana Road Network | `ghana_roads.geojson` (OSM-derived, major roads) | `backend/app/data/ghana_roads.geojson` |
| Known Gold Deposits | Hardcoded seed (14 real West African deposits: Obuasi, Tarkwa, Damang, etc.) | `backend/app/services/mineral_sites_service.py` — `SeedSource` class |

---

### Why These Sources?

Every source had to clear **4 bars**:

1. **Global coverage** — works anywhere, not just one country
2. **Commercial licence** — legally usable in a commercial product
3. **Stable programmatic access** — can be fetched automatically by code
4. **Appropriate resolution** — detailed enough for the decision it informs

> [!TIP]
> **The deliberate design:** Public data is used for *context and weighting*; the user's own survey data is the *primary anomaly evidence*. Regional magnetics at 2 arc-minutes cannot define a drill target and is never asked to. This is why the platform is useful on day one but gets materially better once a customer uploads their own ground or airborne survey.

